ying\n     - R2.2: `-D` - create leading dest directory components, then copy\n     - R2.3: `-b`/`--backup` + `--suffix=SUFFIX` (default `~`) - backup existing dest\n     - R2.4: `-v`/`--verbose` - print each file name as installed\n     - Non-goals: no --strip, no SELinux context\n\n   - **cmd/install/main.go** (read, needs modification)\n     - Existing implementation covers R1.1-R1.4 (copy, -m MODE, -o OWNER, -g GROUP)\n     - Current `options` struct (line 37-41):\n       ```go\n       type options struct {\n           mode  string\n           owner string\n           group string\n       }\n       ```\n     - `main()` (line 43-72): Calls parseArgs, validates operand count, dispatches to installSingle or installMultiple\n     - `installSingle()` (line 92-110): Stats src, handles dir dest, calls copyFile/setMode/setOwnership\n     - `installMultiple()` (line 74-90): Validates dest is dir, iterates sources\n     - `copyFile()` (line 112-130): Opens src, creates dest, io.Copy\n     - `parseArgs()` (line 223-252): Manual flag parser with endOfFlags support\n     - `parseLongFlag()` (line 254-271): Handles --help, --version, --mode=, --owner=, --group=\n     - `parseShortFlags()` (line 273-298): Handles -m, -o, -g, -c (ignored)\n     - `consumeValue()` (line 300-309): Helper to consume flag values from same arg or next arg\n     - `helpText` const (line 20-32): Usage help string - needs updating with new flags\n\n   - **cmd/install/mode.go** (read, no changes needed)\n     - Contains `isOctalMode()`, `evalSymbolic()`, `evalClause()`, `parseWho()`, `parsePerms()`, `applyOp()`, `buildMask()`, `applyEquals()`\n     - These handle the -m MODE flag's symbolic mode parsing\n     - 190 lines, well within file size limits\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - only completed the reading/planning phase.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the `options` struct needs 5 new fields: `directory bool`, `createDirs bool`, `backup bool`, `suffix string`, `